\ Symbol words on variables that need all of Init (review of ops-symbols
\ B3 (c), 2026-11-20; plan row S3, slice S3a-ops C4): Int variables (the
\ max type of `^`: the exponent stays Nat, the base is coerced with no
\ operator above, no homogeneous instance asked of rightact%), numeral bases
\ and exponents of ^ (Init's first candidates) and ∣ (Dvd.dvd). Proved by
\ by-exfalso by-assumption from a hypothesis False, so only the statement's
\ elaboration is under test: tests/front/tactics/decide/check.py --init
\ (make reference-decide-init, part of make daily) requires each accepted
\ with no axiom and its type and value equal to pinned Lean's
\ (goal-layer.lean, theorem si_ID, the Lean statement in the comment above
\ each).

\ n ∣ m
theorem si_p10
  Nat explicit: n  Nat explicit: m  Int explicit: i  Int explicit: j  False explicit: h
  n m ∣
:= by
  by-exfalso
  by-assumption
end si_p10

